  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member whose device uses a non-Gregorian calendar, I want the seasonal icons offered on the same days as the seasonal theme, so that the Noël icons appear in December and the \"revenir à l'icône précédente ?\" question is not asked in the middle of the season.\n\n### Scenario\nOn a device whose calendar is Islamic, Hebrew or Persian, 10 December 2026 is not in month 12 of that calendar: the Noël icons (window 01/12–26/12) are not offered while the Noël theme is; they are offered on days 1–26 of that calendar's 12th month; `AppIconSeasonModel.checkAtLaunch` asks to revert in mid-December; the `<icon>:<year>` token uses that calendar's year.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconOption.swift:32-33` and `:42-43`: `calendar.dateComponents([.month, .day], from: date)` on the calendar it is given.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconSettingsModel.swift:52` and `AppIconSeasonModel.swift:30`: `calendar: Calendar = .current`; the only construction sites (`AppIconSettingsView.swift:13`, `SwiftHFRApp.swift:31`) pass none.\n- By contrast `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/Seasons/NoelCalendar.swift:31` and `SeasonalThemeModel.swift:198` go through `NoelCalendar.gregorian(in:)`: \"season dates and years never follow a Buddhist or Japanese device calendar\".\n- `App/SwiftHFRTests/.../AppIconTestSupport.swift:28` builds a Gregorian calendar for every icon test, so `.current` is never exercised.\n\n### Fix\n`IconWindow.contains` and `lastEndYear` convert through `NoelCalendar.gregorian(in: calendar.timeZone)`, or the two models default to it.\n\n### Test (fails before the fix)\n`iconWindowsAreGregorianWhateverTheDeviceCalendar`: `IconWindow(12,1,12,26).contains(10 Dec 2026, calendar: Calendar(identifier: .islamicUmmAlQura))` is true, and `lastEndYear` on 3 Jan 2027 is 2026.\n\nFoundation's month numbering for these calendars was not run here; the test settles it. Rework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
